WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.334
-It's kind of sweet.
-It's sweet?

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.501
-Yeah, I mean, it should be...

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:08.367
I guess it should be disgusting.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:12.167
Rich, debauched, famous people
just [bleep] on a boat,

00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:15.901
but it's -- it's -- it's --

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.801
It's, like, super wholesome.

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.534
It's -- It's romantic.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:22.634
-Hey, you guys. Welcome back.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:23.734
We're here with
Taylor Schilling,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.067
and that was "Pam &amp; Tommy."
-Yeah.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.567
-And there you are
with Seth Rogen,

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.934
and a lot has been written about
how Sebastian Stan

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.534
and Lily James,
they have to spend so much time

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.567
in the makeup chair to look like
Pam and Tommy.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.100
You guys less so.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.133
-Well, what I would do is I
would go and they'd put a wig on

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:40.334
my head and then
I'd eat a sandwich.

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.934
I'd go back into my trailer
and I'd eat.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.801
-Yeah.
So this was like the dream gig.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.968
-The dream gig.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.033
It took them so much time.
They're so brilliant.

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.100
And they both -- They, you know,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.734
50 bazillion hours
in hair and makeup.

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:58.801
And it was me
and Nick Offerman and Seth --

00:00:58.801 --> 00:00:59.868
[ Laughs ]

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.801
Just put a hat on
and went to crafty.

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:07.501
-You had some very,
very '90s hair.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.300
That's a fantastic look
right there.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.200
-That's right before I ate
my sandwich.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.234
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.901
-That was me alone
in my trailer.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.267
-You're like, "You know what?

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.767
I'm going to get the picture
before the sandwich."

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.734
-I'm gonna get the picture
before the sandwich.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:19.934
-And here's another.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:22.200
That's kind of nicer hair there.
-Aww.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.534
-Did you have some '90s hair

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.467
that you'd be embarrassed by now
personally?

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.400
-Um...

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.200
No. I once, when I was in sixth
grade, tried to cut my hair

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.901
like Maria from
"The Sound of Music."

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.868
-Oh, wow.
-And I was too old to do that.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.334
You know that photograph?
You know that --

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.300
You know that look of
Julie Andrews?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.267
-Yeah.
-It's a bowl cut essentially,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.834
when she's singing
on the mountaintop.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:45.033
-Yes.
-And I was too old to do that.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:48.634
I was like 11. So all the kids
were -- It didn't go over well.

00:01:48.634 --> 00:01:50.701
-Did you do it yourself or did
you have a professional do it?

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:53.167
-I mean, a professional did it,
but, you know...

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.033
-Was it one of those things
that you immediately knew

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.067
when you went to school that
it was the wrong call?

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:01.267
-Yes. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.434
-Or did you know, like,
when you saw...

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.067
-Wait. I have an amazing photo.

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:06.467
The next time I see you,
I'll show you.

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.367
I can see the photo.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.634
I'm sorry I don't have any --
I can't show it now.

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.033
-I like that
you went to show me.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.400
-I thought I had my phone.
-Like this is some magic place

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.934
where whatever you imagine
is here.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:18.133
-I didn't even bring my phone
with me.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:19.601
-Well, you're not supposed to
bring your phone out here.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.567
-No, I know, but I left it
in the haunted house.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.634
I didn't even bring it with me.
It's in Brooklyn.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.033
-Oh, you didn't bring it
to the show?

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.667
-No!
-You can't leave a phone

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:29.267
in a place like that!
-I know! I know!

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:32.133
-The ghosts are gonna be going
crazy on your Instagram.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.400
-Yeah, I didn't even bring it.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.534
-Alright, but you do have
a photo of the haircut?

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:43.133
-Yes, because I -- At the time,
I had glasses and I would

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.834
ride horses, but I'd wear,
like, a Western --

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.767
like a cowboy hat
while I'd ride the horses.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.734
-Uh-huh.
-Not a helmet.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.734
-Okay.
-It's so weird. It's so weird.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:55.367
-So you had a Julie Andrews
haircut, cowboy hat, glasses.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:56.901
-Yes.
-And you thought like,

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.634
"This is gonna rule."
-I thought this was it.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.300
-And then you walked in
the door, like,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.968
waiting for everybody -- like
the record-scratch moment.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:06.067
-Yeah. We're like,
"Not what we were thinking."

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.501
[ Laughter ]
You know, but I hadn't yet found

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.767
the people that would have
thought that was adorable.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.667
-Sometimes you have to live
later in life to find people

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.501
that go for glasses,
cowboy hat, Julie Andrews.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:16.767
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.000
They understand my aesthetic.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.133
-Is it true that you tried to
change your name in the '90s?

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.467
-Oh, yes.
-Okay.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.367
-Yeah, I tried to change my name
in the '90s.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.834
I got tired of being confused
as a boy,

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:32.501
which probably had something to
do with my bowl cut, you know?

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.067
[ Laughter ]
Now that I'm thinking about it.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.167
-You were maybe doing
a lot of things

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.267
that were adding
to the confusion.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:37.701
-I was adding to the confusion.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:40.200
But [bleep] I didn't even really
think of that until right now.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.801
I'm like, "That was probably
because of my haircut."

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.400
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.300
You were, like, saying to
your parents like,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.634
"Why'd you you name me Taylor?"
-"Why'd you name me Taylor?"

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:47.901
-And they're like, "Honey..."

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:49.300
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.968
So I was upset about my name,

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.567
but, really, I was upset about
the bowl cut.

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.334
But I was upset about my name,
so I ch--

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughs ]
I changed it to Tally.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.834
-Tally?
-Yeah.

00:03:58.834 --> 00:03:59.934
-How do you spell Tally?

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.501
-T-A-L-L-Y.
-Okay.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:04.567
-I don't think I knew
what a Tally was,

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:07.067
and I did it for one season of
my soccer league.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.434
-Okay, gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.400
-But these were people that you
had grown up with, right?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.667
It wasn't a new school
or anything.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:12.801
-No. No.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.300
-So you had to --
That's a weird thing --

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.968
-That was really weird too.
-Yeah, when you show up

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.000
and you're like,
"Hey, news flash."

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.467
-"My name's Tally."
-Yeah.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.467
-And it's a weird name.
-Yeah.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:22.701
-I had a song. It'd be like...

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.834
♪ Tally-ho and Ranger Joe ♪

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.601
[ Laughter ]
That was it.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:28.400
-Well, that's helpful.
-♪ Tally-ho and Ranger Joe ♪

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.667
♪ They go together ♪

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.434
-Well, that's good because
when you have a new name,

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.434
I think you almost have to
bring a theme song

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:34.734
to help people remember.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.567
-I can't believe I just
remembered that on TV with you.

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.667
I think it was like,
♪ Tally-ho and Ranger Joe ♪

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.267
♪ They go together,
they should get married ♪

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.067
-And then was there just like
a long silence

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.000
from your soccer team
as they were like, "Okay"?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.634
-They were like,
"Put your sombrero away

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:57.968
and get on the field!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.968 --> 00:04:59.467
-Were you good at soccer?
-No.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.367
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.901
-I wouldn't be sitting here
with you

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.701
if I was good at things
like soccer.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:08.634
-Wait, this is your fallback?

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:09.734
Being bad a soccer?
-Yeah.

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.267
[ Laughter ]
-Your coach took you aside

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:14.133
and was like, "Listen, Taylor,
Tally, I don't know what it is.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:15.701
Soccer's not going to work out,

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.634
but you could be
a talk-show-host guest one day."

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.267
-Yeah, yeah.
-And here you are.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:20.434
-And here I am.
-Turns out your coach was right.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.400
Hey, it is always nothing less

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.501
than a total pleasure
to see you.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:24.734
-Yeah.
-Thanks for being back.

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:26.501
Good luck at that apartment.
It sounds awesome.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:27.734
Please don't invite me over.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:28.868
You guys...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.267
...that's Taylor Schilling.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.634
"Pam &amp; Tommy" is now available
to stream on Hulu.

